{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011LfwF3Vjxj8AWMTixiicX7","type":"tool_result","content":"### Running a component\n\n**Host**:\nThe custom element instance a component's behaviour is attached to. Its\nchildren are light DOM, never a shadow root.\n_Avoid_: root, wrapper, container\n\n**Setup**:\nThe function run once per host when it connects, after refs resolve and\nrequired provided contexts are available.\n_Avoid_: init, mount, constructor\n\n**Setup context**:\nThe object handed to `setup`, carrying the host, prop signals, resolved\nrefs, provided context values, and lifecycle helpers.\n_Avoid_: bare \"context\", ctx (in prose)\n\n**Provided context**:\nA value published by an ancestor host and read by descendants that opt in\nwith `withContexts` or `consume`. Reactive: consumers re-run when the\n12:Web component helper with reactive props, automatic cleanup, and\n869:| `.on(target, type, handler, options?)` | `void` | Add a DOM event listener, auto-removed on disconnect. |\n871:| `.effect(fn)` | `void` | Run an alien-signals effect that auto-tracks the signals it reads. Auto-disposed on disconnect. |\n872:| `.bind(signal, element, options?)` | `void` | Bind a signal to a DOM element property, auto-cleaned on disconnect. |\n873:| `.onCleanup(fn)` | `void` | Register custom teardown to run on disconnect. |\n1101:        // Share with descendants; remove the entry on disconnect.\n1103:        ctx.onCleanup(cleanup)\n1265:Helpers for reading raw attribute strings and running cleanup\n1575:| `token.provide(ctx, value)` | `provide(ctx.host, token, value)`, standalone, returns a cleanup |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b28f79d1-258a-42fe-b5b0-ae14375911e2","uuid":"296258a3-8577-4917-b468-a1a72ac2ac4e","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:08:51.119Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### Running a component\n\n**Host**:\nThe custom element instance a component's behaviour is attached to. Its\nchildren are light DOM, never a shadow root.\n_Avoid_: root, wrapper, container\n\n**Setup**:\nThe function run once per host when it connects, after refs resolve and\nrequired provided contexts are available.\n_Avoid_: init, mount, constructor\n\n**Setup context**:\nThe object handed to `setup`, carrying the host, prop signals, resolved\nrefs, provided context values, and lifecycle helpers.\n_Avoid_: bare \"context\", ctx (in prose)\n\n**Provided context**:\nA value published by an ancestor host and read by descendants that opt in\nwith `withContexts` or `consume`. Reactive: consumers re-run when the\n12:Web component helper with reactive props, automatic cleanup, and\n869:| `.on(target, type, handler, options?)` | `void` | Add a DOM event listener, auto-removed on disconnect. |\n871:| `.effect(fn)` | `void` | Run an alien-signals effect that auto-tracks the signals it reads. Auto-disposed on disconnect. |\n872:| `.bind(signal, element, options?)` | `void` | Bind a signal to a DOM element property, auto-cleaned on disconnect. |\n873:| `.onCleanup(fn)` | `void` | Register custom teardown to run on disconnect. |\n1101:        // Share with descendants; remove the entry on disconnect.\n1103:        ctx.onCleanup(cleanup)\n1265:Helpers for reading raw attribute strings and running cleanup\n1575:| `token.provide(ctx, value)` | `provide(ctx.host, token, value)`, standalone, returns a cleanup |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011LfwF3Vjxj8AWMTixiicX7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
