{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3NCPjLgUaXteeuoBzAv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013DnjPwRjAxhhoZ6FihDxiU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"So an element that is\nmoved, removed and re-inserted in the same tick, keeps its setup and state,\neven in browsers without `moveBefore`.\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,\"\"\"So an element that is\nremoved and re-inserted in the same tick (a move) keeps its setup and\nstate, even in browsers without `moveBefore`.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.rstrip('\\n')+\"\"\"\n\n### Host teardown (`src/factory.ts`)\n\n`disconnectedCallback` only queues a microtask; teardown (running the\ncleanups) happens there if the host is still disconnected. A `_live`\nflag makes `connectedCallback` return early for a host that came back\nbefore teardown, so same-tick moves keep setup state. Tests that check\ncleanup after a removal must `await Promise.resolve()` first. A\nthrowing cleanup now surfaces as an uncaught error, which fails the\ntapout run, so tests for it capture the queued task with the\n`catchTeardown` helper in `test/index.ts`. To force the morph's\n`insertBefore` fallback in Chromium, set `moveBefore` to `undefined` on\nthe parent instance. Tapout always listens on port 8123; `EADDRINUSE`\nmeans another worktree is testing, so retry.\n\"\"\"\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnpm run lint 2>&1 | tail -3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":88003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":794},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"se