{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3NFvEDcavQUjWVmdCmc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Browser suite: with the parent's `moveBefore` shadowed by `undefined`, reordering a keyed list of hosts through a region runs setup once per host and a signal created in setup keeps its value after the reorder.\n[x] Browser suite: moving a host with `insertBefore` directly, then awaiting a microtask, runs no cleanups.\n[x] Browser suite: after a real removal and `await Promise.resolve()`, cleanups have run exactly once.\n[x] Browser suite: removing a host twice before the microtask runs the cleanups once.\n[x] Browser suite: reconnecting a host after its teardown runs setup again (the existing second-connect behaviour still holds).\n[x] All existing disconnect and cleanup tests pass after awaiting a microtask.\n[x] `npm run size` passes, with any raised limit recorded in the size file's comment.\n\nA host that is removed and put back in the same tick now keeps its setup and state. `npm test` passes (297 tests), as do the SSR, build, plugins and CLI suites, lint, typecheck and size. The two hydration suites failed before running any test (details at the end).\n\n**What changed.** In `src/factory.ts`, a host has a `_live` flag. `connectedCallback` returns early if the host is still live. `disconnectedCallback` now only queues a microtask; when it runs, it tears the host down only if the host is still disconnected and still live. That makes a second queued teardown do nothing. `connectedMoveCallback` is still empty. I added a test for each checklist item, each with its own tag name. The move and double-removal tests fail against the old factory, and the reorder test failed before the change (5 setups instead of 3).\n\n**One test contract changed.** Two existing tests called `disconnectedCallback()` directly and caught the error from a throwing cleanup. That error now comes from inside a microtask, so it reaches the page as an uncaught error, and the test runner (tapout) fails the whole run on any such error. I tried stopping it with a capture-phase listener and that did not work. Both tests now use a small `catchTeardown` helper in `test/index.ts`. It swaps `window.queueMicrotask` while the host is removed, runs the queued teardown itself, and returns the first error. The assertions are the same as before, but the tests now depend on the implementation using `queueMicrotask`, which the spec specifies.\n\n**Size.** No limit had to rise. Core measures 4.2 kB against a 4.2 kB limit, so the next feature will likely push it over. The browser templater is 4.56 kB against 4.6 kB.\n\n**Docs.** README (the `builder.setup` section and the `ctx` methods table) and the **Setup** entry in `CONTEXT.md` now say cleanup runs a microtask after disconnect. I added a \"Host teardown\" section to `AGENTS.md` covering the timing, the `catchTeardown` helper, how to force the `insertBefore` fallback, and retrying when port 8123 is busy.\n\n**Hydration suites.** `test:hydration` and `test:hydration-dev` stop while loading the Vite config, with `microtags/build requires \"typescript\" as a peer dependency`. The ESM `dist/vite.js` calls `require('typescript')`, and `require` doesn't exist in ESM. Loading that config never touches `src/factory.ts`, so this isn't caused by this ticket, and I left it alone. It does mean nothing has checked the hydration example with the new teardown timing.\n\nThere are two commits, `cb977d1` (code and tests) and `594ed4e` (docs). My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":723,"cache_read_input_tokens":92314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":723},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b28f79d1-258a-42fe-b5b0-ae14375911e2","uuid":"4b816252-8169-4a9c-bfb3-45ccb131e812","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:10:00.165Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3NFuwc1gdeA4SSHXWyB"}
