o rise. Core measures 4.2 kB against a 4.2 kB limit, so the next feature will likely push it over. The browser templater is 4.56 kB against 4.6 kB.\n\n**Docs.** README (the `builder.setup` section and the `ctx` methods table) and the **Setup** entry in `CONTEXT.md` now say cleanup runs a microtask after disconnect. I added a \"Host teardown\" section to `AGENTS.md` covering the timing, the `catchTeardown` helper, how to force the `insertBefore` fallback, and retrying when port 8123 is busy.\n\n**Hydration suites.** `test:hydration` and `test:hydration-dev` stop while loading the Vite config, with `microtags/build requires \"typescript\" as a peer dependency`. The ESM `dist/vite.js` calls `require('typescript')`, and `require` doesn't exist in ESM. Loading that config never touches `src/factory.ts`, so this isn't caused by this ticket, and I left it alone. It does mean nothing has checked the hydration example with the new teardown timing.\n\nThere are two commits, `cb977d1` (code and tests) and `594ed4e` (docs). My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed.","ttft_ms":2516,"type":"result","duration_ms":242963,"uuid":"d534651f-6417-40aa-bd39-211dc9d7417d","ttft_stream_ms":1721,"time_to_request_ms":94,"first_content_frame_ms":1721,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
